    "origin": "original_seed",
    "prompt": "A library catalogue audit shows how a primary school's entire collection of exactly 200 books is classified into four separate categories: 100 are fiction, 50 are non-fiction, 40 are picture books, and 10 are reference books. To find how many times as many fiction books there are as reference books, a librarian sets up the calculation 100 ÷ 10. What is the value of 100 ÷ 10?",
