    },
    "explanation": "According to the audit, the fiction segment represents 100 books and the reference segment represents only 10 books. Working out 'how many times as many' always means dividing the larger quantity by the smaller quantity. Dividing 100 by 10 gives exactly 10, with nothing left over. Therefore, the fiction collection is 10 times the size of the reference collection.",
